# 2) Asset directories — explicit 404 on miss, NEVER fall through to SPA fallback.
# Without this, deploy-race fetches (Discord/Telegram link previews, admin self-verify,
# search crawlers hitting a URL while CF Pages is mid-build) get rewritten to index.html,
# cached as text/html on edge under /news/<file>.png keys, then persist up to 24h per
# /*.png cache-control rule. Returning a clean 404 keeps the cache uncontaminated; the
# next fetch after deploy completes resolves to the real file.
/news/*       /news/:splat       404
/events/*     /events/:splat     404
/posts/*      /posts/:splat      404
/members/*    /members/:splat    404
/assets/*     /assets/:splat     404

# 3) SPA fallback — every other non-asset path → index.html (200, NOT 301)
/*    /index.html   200
